#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703699 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e2bdff-333f-5ef4-ac82-327989b102b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(1 + 2 e^{3}\\right)}{1 + e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703657} {:answer/id #uuid "34a0f455-5242-5621-b416-d955e570ae49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 + 2 e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703667} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf962f2-ed42-58a5-8453-493799708590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1 + 2 e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703675} {:answer/id #uuid "676b8c76-46df-5412-a5e9-5419a69e3941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 + 5 e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703677} {:answer/id #uuid "a54c6cc1-1720-5e71-b446-82ebaad5f044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 \\left(2 + 3 e^{3}\\right)}{1 + e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703687}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703687} :answer-field/id #uuid "339a1996-dd28-5dac-a7eb-669b3789b711" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122afc4b-fb1f-5781-b892-77b88ce02a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 + e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703656} {:answer/id #uuid "5e332027-eb58-598d-947b-fc44dde4d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1 + 2 e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703676} {:answer/id #uuid "880dac31-d6b8-58be-adcb-4058509030f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 + 3 e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703684} {:answer/id #uuid "ba814d92-de23-5f83-afb7-23eb26aac121" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1 + e^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703694} {:answer/id #uuid "bd311ce9-6df4-51e3-97d5-beac836acd20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703695}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703676} :answer-field/id #uuid "b295afa0-7a7b-5399-b0c9-a308a7b5a4a8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d5a098ac-1507-532c-ad17-f6f7d3354ef9" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=x^{2} y + \\ln{\\left(e^{x^{2} + y} + 1 \\right)},\n$$\n\nevaluate both partial derivatives at $(1,2)$.\n\n$f_x(1,2)=$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\n$f_y(1,2)=$\n\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as constant and differentiate with respect to $x$. Apply the chain rule, and the sum and constant multiple rules where needed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=x^{2} + y\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&=2 x\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\ln(1+e^u)&=\\frac{1}{1+e^u}\\cdot e^u\\cdot\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(x^{2} y\\right)&=2 x y\\\\\nf_x(x,y)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(2 x\\right)+\\left(2 x y\\right)\\\\\n&=2 x y + \\frac{2 x e^{x^{2} + y}}{e^{x^{2} + y} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=1$ and $y=2$ after differentiating. The inner input is\n\n$$\nu_0=\\left(1\\right)^{2} + \\left(2\\right)=3.\n$$\n\nUsing this value in the chain factors gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(1,2)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u_0}}{e^{u_0} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(2\\right)+\\left(4\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}\\right)\\cdot\\left(2\\right)+\\left(4\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{2 \\left(2 + 3 e^{3}\\right)}{1 + e^{3}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTreat $x$ as constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Apply the chain rule, and the sum and constant multiple rules where needed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=x^{2} + y\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}&=1\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\ln(1+e^u)&=\\frac{1}{1+e^u}\\cdot e^u\\cdot\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(x^{2} y\\right)&=x^{2}\\\\\nf_y(x,y)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(x^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=x^{2} + \\frac{e^{x^{2} + y}}{e^{x^{2} + y} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=1$ and $y=2$ after differentiating. The inner input is\n\n$$\nu_0=\\left(1\\right)^{2} + \\left(2\\right)=3.\n$$\n\nUsing this value in the chain factors gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(1,2)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u_0}}{e^{u_0} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(1\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(1\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{1 + 2 e^{3}}{1 + e^{3}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese derivatives apply for all real $x,y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703779 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137d5731-be82-5061-84e4-ad3aa79d9eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1 + 2 e^{2}}{1 + e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703766} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6d0c3d-ca5f-5a83-959d-19956b96c957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5 + 4 e^{2}}{2 \\left(1 + e^{2}\\right)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703783} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa9a357-6689-5b5c-bf4d-349633a5129c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2 e^{2}}{1 + e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703803} {:answer/id #uuid "f79cafe8-ad2c-5cd4-a238-712a6b7b10db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{-2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703811} {:answer/id #uuid "f7da1ee4-432d-5cba-a574-097ba553ce37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3 + 2 e^{2}}{1 + e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703812}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703812} :answer-field/id #uuid "05772023-c67b-5b15-9ec0-0f29e2464db6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007c0e75-2d01-5ad0-83a2-2b95a99418d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{1 + e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703763} {:answer/id #uuid "338ea97e-06fa-5c2f-b746-627d2d7078e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{4}{e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703768} {:answer/id #uuid "c476ec8f-de55-5ced-8222-96f47cb52600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1 + e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703798} {:answer/id #uuid "cd450952-57ac-582b-b20c-3598fa7b1bd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{4 e^{2}}{1 + e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703801} {:answer/id #uuid "dd102e97-ba8d-56a0-884a-8e8f5ade546d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{8}{1 + e^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703808}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703763} :answer-field/id #uuid "668a5b94-94a0-52ce-84a9-681cdb2846f1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "75332933-81f5-5b3e-9643-b155acc35353" :question/problem "For the function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=2 x y^{2} + \\ln{\\left(e^{x - 2 y^{2}} + 1 \\right)},\n$$\n\nevaluate both partial derivatives at $(0,1)$.\n\n$f_x(0,1)=$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\n$f_y(0,1)=$\n\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Treat $y$ as constant and differentiate with respect to $x$. Apply the chain rule, and the sum and constant multiple rules where needed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=x - 2 y^{2}\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&=1\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\ln(1+e^u)&=\\frac{1}{1+e^u}\\cdot e^u\\cdot\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(2 x y^{2}\\right)&=2 y^{2}\\\\\nf_x(x,y)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(2 y^{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=2 y^{2} + \\frac{e^{x - 2 y^{2}}}{e^{x - 2 y^{2}} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=0$ and $y=1$ after differentiating. The inner input is\n\n$$\nu_0=\\left(0\\right) - 2 \\left(1\\right)^{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing this value in the chain factors gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x(0,1)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u_0}}{e^{u_0} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{1}{\\left(e^{-2} + 1\\right) e^{2}}\\right)\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\left(2\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac{3 + 2 e^{2}}{1 + e^{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTreat $x$ as constant and differentiate with respect to $y$. Apply the chain rule, and the sum and constant multiple rules where needed.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu&=x - 2 y^{2}\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}&=- 4 y\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\ln(1+e^u)&=\\frac{1}{1+e^u}\\cdot e^u\\cdot\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\n\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(2 x y^{2}\\right)&=4 x y\\\\\nf_y(x,y)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u}}{e^{u} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(- 4 y\\right)+\\left(4 x y\\right)\\\\\n&=4 x y - \\frac{4 y e^{x - 2 y^{2}}}{e^{x - 2 y^{2}} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=0$ and $y=1$ after differentiating. The inner input is\n\n$$\nu_0=\\left(0\\right) - 2 \\left(1\\right)^{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nUsing this value in the chain factors gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y(0,1)&=\\left(\\frac{e^{u_0}}{e^{u_0} + 1}\\right)\\cdot\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\left(\\frac{1}{\\left(e^{-2} + 1\\right) e^{2}}\\right)\\cdot\\left(-4\\right)+\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=- \\frac{4}{1 + e^{2}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese derivatives apply for all real $x,y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186703792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58d9c54c-5364-5325-b1f3-ea264676a239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{1 + e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186703775} {:answer/id #uuid "96a7ea34-6cd0-52b9-aaa4-31e429487c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175